<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georges-Eugène Haussmann</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1809">1809</a>–<a href="/years/1891">1891</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Baron Haussmann</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georges-Eugène Haussmann was a French administrator who, as prefect of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> from 1853 to 1870 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a>, directed the rebuilding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. His works cut wide boulevards through the medieval centre, created parks, a new water supply and sewers, and imposed uniform façades along the streets. The cost and the destruction of old quarters made him controversial, and he was dismissed in January 1870, but his plan still shapes the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/georges-eugene-haussmann.jpg" alt="Georges-Eugène Haussmann" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown . Stitch and restoration by Jebulon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georges-Eug%C3%A8ne_Haussmann_-_BNF_Gallica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
